{"CLs":[{"__type":"ST","Var":"Info_General"}],"CMT":"The sensor object is used for digital AND analogic sensor.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aOn IAG,  digital sensor will appear as a round LED, while the analog version will be a square filled according to the percentage of the analog input.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aIn commissioning, you have several possibility:\u000d\u000a- Digital: I check every edge of the input and store theme in \"Min\/Max\" datas. With this, you can change the state of a sensor, and check if you have\u000d\u000a               a feedback on the IAG\u000d\u000a- Analog: You can use a teaching function if you need. During the teaching, i will store the maximum and the minimum value to define 0-100%\u000d\u000a- All visual feedback on IAG are not filtred!","LRI":1,"RRI":2,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"P_On"},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":1,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_ID_Simple"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Input","IO":true,"Ix":2,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.IN_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Enable"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Use_Debounce","Ix":3,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.Debounce_Used"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"DebounceTime","Ix":4,"Type":"TIME","Var":"debounceTime"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Use_LivingTime","Ix":5,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.LivingTime_Used"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"LivingTime","Ix":6,"Type":"TIME","Var":"livingTime"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Commissioning","Ix":7,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Commissioning"}],"Ix":14,"Name":"Sensor_Simple","Out":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":8,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_ID_Simple"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Input","IO":true,"Ix":9,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.IN_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"}],"UD":true,"X":1,"Var":"configSimple"},{"__type":"F","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"EN"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"In","Ix":10,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.Debounce_Time"}],"Ix":15,"Name":"REAL_TO_TIME","Out":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"","Ix":11,"Type":"TIME","Var":"debounceTime"}],"UD":true,"X":2},{"__type":"F","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"EN"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"In","Ix":12,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.LivingTime_Time"}],"Ix":16,"Name":"REAL_TO_TIME","Out":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"","Ix":13,"Type":"TIME","Var":"livingTime"}],"UD":true,"X":2,"Y":1}],"CMT":"###   Digital sensor   #############################################################################\u000a\u000d\u000aThis object can be used for every machine sensor. The basic configuration provides two options:\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a1. Debounce: Define a minimum debounce time. The input must remain ON during this time before `Sensor.Detection` rises.\u000d\u000a   -> This option can be used to filter input noise or to wait a defined amount of time before raising an alarm.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a2. LivingTime: Force the output to remain ON after the input falls (TOF behavior).\u000d\u000a    -> This option can be used to keep an alarm active for a minimum amount of time.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aChronogram:\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aInput        __________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|____________________|¯¯|___|¯¯|__|¯¯|______|¯¯|______|¯¯|___|¯¯|__|¯¯|__|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|__________________________________________________\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aOutput     ___________________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|_____________\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a                                |-- 0.3 --|                                                                                                                                                     |------------------ 3s ----------------| \u000d\u000a","LRI":17,"RRI":18,"VLs":[{"Ix":19,"X":2}]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"P_On"},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":3,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_ID_TriState"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Input","IO":true,"Ix":4,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.IN_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Enable"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"TimeDetection","Ix":5,"Type":"TIME","Var":"transitionTime"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Commissioning","Ix":6,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Commissioning"}],"Ix":9,"Name":"Sensor_TriState","Out":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":7,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_ID_TriState"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Input","IO":true,"Ix":8,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.IN_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"}],"UD":true,"X":1,"Var":"configTriState"},{"__type":"F","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"EN"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"In","Ix":1,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.TransitionTime"}],"Ix":10,"Name":"REAL_TO_TIME","Out":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"","Ix":2,"Type":"TIME","Var":"transitionTime"}],"UD":true,"X":2}],"CMT":"TriState mode is intended for blinking sensors detecting moving products.\u000a\u000aThree states are available:\u000a\u000a- Transition: Normal behavior. Products are moving and signal transitions are detected.\u000a- NoDetection: No product detected during the configured time.\u000a- Detection: Sensor remains continuously active without transitions during the configured time, indicating a blocked product.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aChronogram:\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aInput        __________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|____________________|¯¯|___|¯¯|__|¯¯|______|¯¯|______|¯¯|___|¯¯|__|¯¯|__|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|__________________________________________________\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aDo detect  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|______________________________________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|___________________________________________________________________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aDetection  ___________________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|___________________________________________________________________________|¯|__________________________________________________\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aTransition   ________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|__________________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|__________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|_|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|________________________________________\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a                                |-- 0.3 --|                             |-- 0.3 --|                                                                                        |-- 0.3 --|  |-- 0.3 --|\u000d\u000a","LRI":11,"RRI":12,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"P_On"},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":3,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_ID_ToAnalog"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Input","IO":true,"Ix":4,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.IN_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Run"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Enable","Ix":5,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"True"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Pulse","Ix":6,"Type":"TIME","Var":"pulseTime"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Level_On","Ix":7,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.ToAnalog_On"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Level_Off","Ix":8,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.ToAnalog_Off"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Commissioning","Ix":9,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Commissioning"}],"Ix":13,"Name":"Sensor_ToAnalog","Out":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":10,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_ID_ToAnalog"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Input","IO":true,"Ix":11,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Sensors.IN_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"AnalogOut","Ix":12,"Type":"REAL","Var":""}],"UD":true,"X":1,"Var":"configToAnalog"},{"__type":"F","In":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"EN"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"In","Ix":1,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.ToAnalog_Pulse"}],"Ix":14,"Name":"REAL_TO_TIME","Out":[{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"","Ix":2,"Type":"TIME","Var":"pulseTime"}],"UD":true,"X":2}],"CMT":"This object converts a pulsed digital signal into an analog value.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aDuring the configured Pulse period, the object measures how long the input remains ON and computes a percentage value.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aExamples:\u000d\u000a- Input ON during 100% of Pulse -> Analog = 100%\u000d\u000a- Input ON during 50% of Pulse -> Analog = 50%\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aThe computed value is available in `MyObj.Analog` or `AnalogOut`.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aDefining `Level_On` and `Level_Off` enables the digital output with hysteresis behavior: SET when the analog value rises above `Level_On`, RESET when it falls below `Level_Off`.\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aChronogram:\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aInput        __________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|____________________|¯¯|___|¯¯|__|¯¯|______|¯¯|______|¯¯|___|¯¯|__|¯¯|__|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|__________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|______________________________\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aPulse       __________||_________________||_________________||_________________||_________________||_________________||_________________||_________________||_________________||__________\u000d\u000a                               |------- 1s -------| \u000d\u000aAnalog           0%   |           100%        |           70%        |            9%          |            42%        |           38%        |           92%         |            50%        |             0%        |           0%  \u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aOutput     _________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|______________________________________________________|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|______________________________\u000d\u000a","LRI":15,"RRI":16,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"ST","Var":"Info_ToDo"}],"CMT":"Creating a FB call \"Sensor_ToSpeed\" to convert a digital input to a speed.\u000d\u000aCan be usefull to convert a basic digital measurment to a speed (Ex: BDA traversing or DBV with break).\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aWe need an input parameter for the distance travel every rising edge, and some filtring (Avg, lower speed control, etc....)","LRI":1,"RRI":2,"VLs":[]}
{"CLs":[{"__type":"LD","Var":"P_On"},{"__type":"FB","In":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":1,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_AD_Analog"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Integer","IO":true,"Ix":2,"Type":"INT","Var":"Sensors.AD_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"Enable"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Input_Min","Ix":3,"Type":"REAL","Var":"0"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Input_Max","Ix":4,"Type":"REAL","Var":"4000"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Output_Min","Ix":5,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.AD_OutMin"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Output_Max","Ix":6,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.AD_OutMax"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Offset","Ix":7,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.AD_OutOffset"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Unit","Ix":8,"Type":"STRING[6]","Var":"'%'"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Average","Ix":9,"Type":"REAL","Var":"Sensors.AD_Average"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Use_Teaching","Ix":10,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"true"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Use_Limit","Ix":11,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"true"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Commissioning","Ix":12,"Type":"BOOL","Var":"Commissioning"}],"Ix":16,"Name":"Sensor_Analog","Out":[{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"MySensor","IO":true,"Ix":13,"Type":"OBJ\\SENSOR\\BASE","Var":"Sensor_AD_Analog"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"IO_Integer","IO":true,"Ix":14,"Type":"INT","Var":"Sensors.AD_Sensor"},{"__type":"PF","Arg":"ENO"},{"__type":"PRM","Arg":"Output","Ix":15,"Type":"REAL","Var":""}],"UD":true,"X":1,"Var":"configAnalog"}],"CMT":"###   Analog sensor   ############################################################################\u000d\u000a\u000d\u000aAnalog sensors use the same structure. Only the configuration FB changes.\u000a\u000aTwo configuration FBs are available:\u000a- `Sensor_Analog` for standard analog inputs (`INT`).\u000a- `Sensor_Analog_IOLink` for analog values received from an IO-Link sensor (`ARRAY[0..1] OF BYTE`).\u000a\u000aThe FB directly scales the input value using `Input_Min`, `Input_Max`, `Output_Min`, and `Output_Max`.\u000aIn this example, an analog input value of `0..4000` is converted to `0..100%`.\u000a\u000aThe output value can be adjusted using `Offset`.\u000a\u000aThe `Unit` parameter is only used to display information on the IAG.\u000a\u000aIf needed, the FB can directly average the signal. Define the moving average size with `Average`.\u000a\u000a`Use_Teaching` allows the operator, during commissioning, to update `Input_Min` and `Input_Max` from the HMI using a teaching function.\u000a\u000aBy default, scaling is not limited to `Output_Min` and `Output_Max`, but the output can be constrained by enabling `Use_Limit`.","LRI":17,"RRI":18,"VLs":[]}
